## 3. Migration Strategy

### 3.1 Phased Migration Approach

The migration will be implemented in phases to minimize disruption and allow for incremental validation:

#### Phase 1: Setup and Environment
1. Initialize Next.js project with TypeScript
2. Set up project structure and dependencies
3. Configure environment variables and validation
4. Create shared utility functions

#### Phase 2: API Client Migration
1. Convert Notion API client to TypeScript
2. Convert GitHub API client to TypeScript
3. Implement ChromaDB client
4. Create type definitions for all API responses

#### Phase 3: Route Handlers Migration
1. Implement API routes for GitHub endpoints
2. Implement API routes for Notion database endpoints
3. Implement API routes for Notion memory endpoints
4. Implement API routes for Notion page endpoints
5. Implement health check endpoints

#### Phase 4: ChromaDB Integration
1. Design ChromaDB collections and schemas
2. Implement migration utilities for Notion memory to ChromaDB
3. Create ChromaDB query utilities
4. Update memory endpoints to use ChromaDB instead of Notion

#### Phase 5: Testing and Validation
1. Create end-to-end tests for all endpoints
2. Validate performance with load tests
3. Verify compatibility with existing clients

#### Phase 6: Deployment and Switchover
1. Set up deployment infrastructure
2. Deploy staging environment
3. Perform final validation
4. Switch production traffic to new system

### 3.2 Detailed Migration Steps

#### Environment Setup

```bash
# Create new Next.js project with TypeScript
npx create-next-app@latest --typescript my-nextjs-app

# Install dependencies
cd my-nextjs-app
npm install @notionhq/client octokit chromadb zod marked pdf-lib

# Copy environment variables
cp /path/to/old/.env .env.local
```

