```bash
# Windows
sc query MongoDB

# macOS/Linux
brew services list  # If installed via Homebrew
systemctl status mongod  # If installed as systemd service
```

### Configuration

Create a MongoDB configuration file `mongodb.conf`:

```yaml
# mongodb.conf
storage:
  dbPath: ./mongo-data
  journal:
    enabled: true
systemLog:
  destination: file
  path: ./mongo-data/mongodb.log
  logAppend: true
net:
  bindIp: 127.0.0.1
  port: 27017
```

### Security Setup

Create a MongoDB admin user:

```javascript
// Run in mongo shell
use admin
db.createUser({
  user: "adminUser",
  pwd: "securePassword",
  roles: [{ role: "userAdminAnyDatabase", db: "admin" }]
})
```

Add this user to your `.env` file (see section 6).

### Connection Testing

Test your MongoDB connection:

```javascript
// test-mongo-connection.js
const { MongoClient } = require('mongodb');

async function testConnection() {
  const uri = "mongodb://localhost:27017";
  const client = new MongoClient(uri);

  try {
    await client.connect();
    console.log("Connected successfully to MongoDB");

    const dbs = await client.db().admin().listDatabases();
    console.log("Databases:", dbs.databases.map(db => db.name));
  } catch (e) {
    console.error("Connection error:", e);
  } finally {
    await client.close();
  }
}

testConnection();
```

