<a id="introduction"></a>
## 1. Introduction to ChromaDB and Vector Embeddings

### What are Vector Embeddings?

Vector embeddings are numerical representations of data (text, images, etc.) in a high-dimensional space where similar items are positioned closer together. These embeddings capture semantic meaning and relationships between data points, making them powerful for:

- Semantic search (finding content based on meaning rather than exact keyword matches)
- Content recommendation systems
- Data clustering and classification
- AI-powered question answering

![Vector Embedding Visualization](https://i.imgur.com/example.png)

*Conceptual diagram: Text converted to vector embeddings in high-dimensional space, with similar concepts clustered together*

### Why ChromaDB?

ChromaDB is an open-source vector database designed specifically for storing and querying embedding vectors efficiently. It offers:

- **Simplicity**: Easy-to-use API with Python and JavaScript clients
- **Performance**: Optimized for fast similarity searches
- **Flexibility**: Support for multiple embedding models and similarity metrics
- **Persistence**: Options for in-memory, disk-based, or client-server architectures
- **Integration**: Works well with popular embedding providers like OpenAI and Anthropic

For your Next.js application structure, ChromaDB will serve as the storage and retrieval mechanism for AI-generated embeddings of your lesson content, blog posts, and other textual data. This enables semantic search, content recommendations, and other AI-powered features.

<a id="installation"></a>
## 2. Installation and Environment Setup

### Package Installation

First, add ChromaDB and related dependencies to your project:

```bash
npm install chromadb langchain @langchain/openai @langchain/anthropic
```

For TypeScript type definitions:

```bash
npm install --save-dev @types/chromadb
```

### Environment Variables

Add the following environment variables to your `.env` file:

```
# ChromaDB Configuration
CHROMA_HOST=localhost
CHROMA_PORT=8000
CHROMA_COLLECTION_NAME=content_embeddings

# Embedding API Keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key

# Path Configuration
CHROMA_DATA_PATH=./chroma-data
```

Also update your `.env.template` file to include these variables (without actual values) for reference.

### Docker Configuration (Optional)

For a more isolated setup, you can run ChromaDB in a Docker container. Create a `docker-compose.yml` file in your project root:

```yaml
version: '3.9'
services:
  chromadb:
    image: ghcr.io/chroma-core/chroma:latest
    volumes:
      - ./chroma-data:/chroma/chroma-data
    ports:
      - "8000:8000"
    environment:
      - CHROMA_DB_IMPL=duckdb+parquet
      - PERSIST_DIRECTORY=/chroma/chroma-data
```

Start the ChromaDB server with:

```bash
docker-compose up -d chromadb
```

<a id="client-configuration"></a>
## 3. ChromaDB Client Configuration

Create the ChromaDB client configuration in `/lib/chroma/client.ts`:

```typescript
// /lib/chroma/client.ts
import { ChromaClient, Collection } from 'chromadb';

// Environment variables with defaults for safety
const CHROMA_HOST = process.env.CHROMA_HOST || 'localhost';
const CHROMA_PORT = parseInt(process.env.CHROMA_PORT || '8000', 10);
const COLLECTION_NAME = process.env.CHROMA_COLLECTION_NAME || 'content_embeddings';

// Singleton pattern for ChromaDB client
let client: ChromaClient | null = null;
let collection: Collection | null = null;

/**
 * Get or initialize the ChromaDB client
 */
export async function getChromaClient(): Promise<ChromaClient> {
  if (!client) {
    client = new ChromaClient({
      path: `http://${CHROMA_HOST}:${CHROMA_PORT}`,
    });

    console.log(`Connected to ChromaDB at ${CHROMA_HOST}:${CHROMA_PORT}`);
  }
  return client;
}

/**
 * Get or create the main content collection
 */
export async function getCollection(): Promise<Collection> {
  if (!collection) {
    const client = await getChromaClient();

    // Check if collection exists
    const collections = await client.listCollections();

    if (collections.includes(COLLECTION_NAME)) {
      collection = await client.getCollection({
        name: COLLECTION_NAME,
      });
      console.log(`Using existing collection: ${COLLECTION_NAME}`);
    } else {
      // Create new collection with default settings
      collection = await client.createCollection({
        name: COLLECTION_NAME,
        metadata: { 
          description: 'Content embeddings for lessons, blog posts, and sessions'
        }
      });
      console.log(`Created new collection: ${COLLECTION_NAME}`);
    }
  }

  return collection;
}

/**
 * Resets the collection (use with caution, primarily for development)
 */
export async function resetCollection(): Promise<void> {
  const client = await getChromaClient();
  const collections = await client.listCollections();

  if (collections.includes(COLLECTION_NAME)) {
    await client.deleteCollection({ name: COLLECTION_NAME });
    console.log(`Deleted collection: ${COLLECTION_NAME}`);
  }

  // Reset collection reference
  collection = null;

  // Recreate collection
  await getCollection();
}

/**
 * Health check function to verify ChromaDB connection
 */
export async function isChromaHealthy(): Promise<boolean> {
  try {
    const client = await getChromaClient();
    await client.heartbeat();
    return true;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('ChromaDB health check failed:', error);
    return false;
  }
}
```

This client configuration provides:
- A singleton pattern for the ChromaDB client and collection
- Collection creation if not exists
- Functions for managing the collection lifecycle
- A health check function for verifying the connection

<a id="embedding-generation"></a>
## 4. Embedding Generation Implementation

Now, let's implement the embedding generation in `/lib/chroma/embed.ts`:

```typescript
// /lib/chroma/embed.ts
import { getCollection } from './client';
import { getOpenAIEmbedding } from '../ai/openai';
import { getAnthropicEmbedding } from '../ai/anthropic';

// Types for content to be embedded
type EmbeddableContent = {
  id: string;
  text: string;
  type: 'lesson' | 'blog' | 'session';
  metadata?: Record<string, any>;
};

// Embedding providers
export enum EmbeddingProvider {
  OPENAI = 'openai',
  ANTHROPIC = 'anthropic',
}

/**
 * Generate embeddings for a single content item
 */
export async function generateEmbedding(
  content: EmbeddableContent,
  provider: EmbeddingProvider = EmbeddingProvider.OPENAI
): Promise<number[]> {
  try {
    // Choose embedding provider based on parameter
    let embedding: number[];

    switch (provider) {
      case EmbeddingProvider.ANTHROPIC:
        embedding = await getAnthropicEmbedding(content.text);
        break;
      case EmbeddingProvider.OPENAI:
      default:
        embedding = await getOpenAIEmbedding(content.text);
        break;
    }

    return embedding;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`Error generating embedding for ${content.id}:`, error);
    throw new Error(`Failed to generate embedding: ${(error as Error).message}`);
  }
}

/**
 * Store content with its embedding in ChromaDB
 */
export async function storeEmbedding(
  content: EmbeddableContent,
  provider: EmbeddingProvider = EmbeddingProvider.OPENAI
): Promise<void> {
  try {
    const collection = await getCollection();
    const embedding = await generateEmbedding(content, provider);

    // Prepare metadata with content type and other metadata
    const metadata = {
      type: content.type,
      ...content.metadata,
    };

    // Add or update item in collection
    await collection.upsert({
      ids: [content.id],
      embeddings: [embedding],
      metadatas: [metadata],
      documents: [content.text],
    });

    console.log(`Stored embedding for ${content.type} with ID: ${content.id}`);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`Error storing embedding for ${content.id}:`, error);
    throw new Error(`Failed to store embedding: ${(error as Error).message}`);
  }
}

/**
 * Batch process multiple content items
 */
export async function batchProcessEmbeddings(
  contents: EmbeddableContent[],
  provider: EmbeddingProvider = EmbeddingProvider.OPENAI
): Promise<void> {
  try {
    const collection = await getCollection();

    // Process in batches of 10 to avoid rate limits
    const BATCH_SIZE = 10;

    for (let i = 0; i < contents.length; i += BATCH_SIZE) {
      const batch = contents.slice(i, i + BATCH_SIZE);

      // Generate embeddings in parallel for the batch
      const embeddingPromises = batch.map(content => 
        generateEmbedding(content, provider)
      );

      const embeddings = await Promise.all(embeddingPromises);

      // Prepare data for batch upsert
      const ids = batch.map(content => content.id);
      const metadatas = batch.map(content => ({
        type: content.type,
        ...content.metadata,
      }));
      const documents = batch.map(content => content.text);

      // Batch upsert to ChromaDB
      await collection.upsert({
        ids,
        embeddings,
        metadatas,
        documents,
      });

      console.log(`Processed batch ${i / BATCH_SIZE + 1} of ${Math.ceil(contents.length / BATCH_SIZE)}`);
    }

    console.log(`Successfully processed ${contents.length} content items`);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error in batch processing:', error);
    throw new Error(`Failed to batch process embeddings: ${(error as Error).message}`);
  }
}

/**
 * Delete embeddings for specified content IDs
 */
export async function deleteEmbeddings(contentIds: string[]): Promise<void> {
  try {
    const collection = await getCollection();
    await collection.delete({ ids: contentIds });
    console.log(`Deleted embeddings for ${contentIds.length} content items`);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error deleting embeddings:', error);
    throw new Error(`Failed to delete embeddings: ${(error as Error).message}`);
  }
}
```

This implementation provides:
- Functions for generating and storing embeddings
- Support for multiple embedding providers (OpenAI and Anthropic)
- Batch processing to handle multiple content items efficiently
- Error handling for embedding generation and storage

<a id="vector-search"></a>
## 5. Vector Search Query Creation

Now, let's implement vector search queries in `/lib/chroma/queries.ts`:

```typescript
// /lib/chroma/queries.ts
import { getCollection } from './client';
import { generateEmbedding, EmbeddingProvider } from './embed';

/**
 * Search for similar content based on a query string
 */
export async function searchByText(
  queryText: string,
  options: {
    provider?: EmbeddingProvider;
    limit?: number;
    contentTypes?: Array<'lesson' | 'blog' | 'session'>;
    minScore?: number;
  } = {}
): Promise<any[]> {
  try {
    const { 
      provider = EmbeddingProvider.OPENAI, 
      limit = 5, 
      contentTypes,
      minScore = 0.7
    } = options;

    // Generate embedding for the query text
    const queryEmbedding = await generateEmbedding(
      { id: 'query', text: queryText, type: 'lesson' },
      provider
    );

    const collection = await getCollection();

    // Prepare where clause if content types are specified
    const whereClause = contentTypes ? { type: { $in: contentTypes } } : undefined;

    // Search for similar content
    const results = await collection.query({
      queryEmbeddings: [queryEmbedding],
      nResults: limit,
      where: whereClause,
    });

    // Process and format the results
    const processedResults = [];

    if (results.ids && results.ids.length > 0 && results.ids[0].length > 0) {
      for (let i = 0; i < results.ids[0].length; i++) {
        // Calculate similarity score (dot product is returned between -1 and 1)
        // Normalize to 0-1 scale where 1 is perfect match
        const score = results.distances && results.distances[0]
          ? 1 - results.distances[0][i] / 2 // Convert distance to similarity
          : 0;

        // Only include results above minimum score
        if (score >= minScore) {
          processedResults.push({
            id: results.ids[0][i],
            text: results.documents && results.documents[0] ? results.documents[0][i] : '',
            metadata: results.metadatas && results.metadatas[0] ? results.metadatas[0][i] : {},
            score: score,
          });
        }
      }
    }

    return processedResults;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error searching content by text:', error);
    throw new Error(`Search failed: ${(error as Error).message}`);
  }
}

/**
 * Search for similar content based on another content ID
 */
export async function searchBySimilarContent(
  contentId: string,
  options: {
    limit?: number;
    contentTypes?: Array<'lesson' | 'blog' | 'session'>;
    excludeSelf?: boolean;
    minScore?: number;
  } = {}
): Promise<any[]> {
  try {
    const { 
      limit = 5, 
      contentTypes,
      excludeSelf = true,
      minScore = 0.7
    } = options;

    const collection = await getCollection();

    // Get the embedding for the referenced content
    const contentResult = await collection.get({
      ids: [contentId],
      include: ['embeddings'],
    });

    if (!contentResult.embeddings || contentResult.embeddings.length === 0) {
      throw new Error(`Content with ID ${contentId} not found or has no embedding`);
    }

    // Use the retrieved embedding for similarity search
    const queryEmbedding = contentResult.embeddings[0];

    // Build where clause based on options
    let whereClause: any = {};

    if (contentTypes) {
      whereClause.type = { $in: contentTypes };
    }

    if (excludeSelf) {
      whereClause.$id = { $ne: contentId };
    }

    // If whereClause is empty, set to undefined
    whereClause = Object.keys(whereClause).length > 0 ? whereClause : undefined;

    // Search for similar content
    const results = await collection.query({
      queryEmbeddings: [queryEmbedding],
      nResults: limit,
      where: whereClause,
    });

    // Process and format the results
    const processedResults = [];

    if (results.ids && results.ids.length > 0 && results.ids[0].length > 0) {
      for (let i = 0; i < results.ids[0].length; i++) {
        // Calculate similarity score (normalize distance to 0-1 similarity)
        const score = results.distances && results.distances[0]
          ? 1 - results.distances[0][i] / 2
          : 0;

        // Only include results above minimum score
        if (score >= minScore) {
          processedResults.push({
            id: results.ids[0][i],
            text: results.documents && results.documents[0] ? results.documents[0][i] : '',
            metadata: results.metadatas && results.metadatas[0] ? results.metadatas[0][i] : {},
            score: score,
          });
        }
      }
    }

    return processedResults;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error searching for similar content:', error);
    throw new Error(`Similarity search failed: ${(error as Error).message}`);
  }
}

/**
 * Find content by metadata properties
 */
export async function findByMetadata(
  metadataQuery: Record<string, any>,
  options: {
    limit?: number;
    includeText?: boolean;
  } = {}
): Promise<any[]> {
  try {
    const { limit = 100, includeText = true } = options;

    const collection = await getCollection();

    // Retrieve content based on metadata
    const results = await collection.get({
      where: metadataQuery,
      limit: limit,
      include: includeText ? ['documents', 'metadatas'] : ['metadatas'],
    });

    // Process and format the results
    const processedResults = [];

    if (results.ids && results.ids.length > 0) {
      for (let i = 0; i < results.ids.length; i++) {
        processedResults.push({
          id: results.ids[i],
          text: includeText && results.documents ? results.documents[i] : '',
          metadata: results.metadatas ? results.metadatas[i] : {},
        });
      }
    }

    return processedResults;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error finding content by metadata:', error);
    throw new Error(`Metadata search failed: ${(error as Error).message}`);
  }
}
```

This implementation provides:
- Text-based semantic search
- Similar content search based on another content item
- Metadata-based search for filtering content
- Score filtering to ensure quality results
- Content type filtering

<a id="api-integration"></a>
## 6. Integration with OpenAI and Anthropic APIs

Now, let's implement the API integrations for generating embeddings in `/lib/ai/openai.ts` and `/lib/ai/anthropic.ts`:

```typescript
// /lib/ai/openai.ts
import OpenAI from 'openai';

// Initialize OpenAI client
const openai = new OpenAI({
  apiKey: process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY,
});

/**
 * Generate embeddings using OpenAI's embedding model
 */
export async function getOpenAIEmbedding(text: string): Promise<number[]> {
  try {
    // Use newer text-embedding-3-small model for better performance
    const response = await openai.embeddings.create({
      model: 'text-embedding-3-small',
      input: text,
    });

    // Return the embedding vector
    return response.data[0].embedding;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('OpenAI embedding error:', error);
    throw new Error(`OpenAI embedding failed: ${(error as Error).message}`);
  }
}

/**
 * Truncate long texts to fit within token limits
 * OpenAI's embedding models have an 8191 token limit
 */
export function truncateForEmbedding(text: string, maxLength = 8000): string {
  // Simple truncation by character count
  // For production, consider more sophisticated truncation based on token count
  if (text.length <= maxLength) {
    return text;
  }

  return text.substring(0, maxLength);
}
```

```typescript
// /lib/ai/anthropic.ts
import Anthropic from '@anthropic-ai/sdk';

// Initialize Anthropic client
const anthropic = new Anthropic({
  apiKey: process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
});

/**
 * Generate embeddings using Anthropic's embedding model
 */
export async function getAnthropicEmbedding(text: string): Promise<number[]> {
  try {
    // Call Anthropic's embedding API
    const response = await anthropic.embeddings.create({
      model: 'claude-3-haiku-20240307',
      input: truncateForEmbedding(text),
    });

    // Return the embedding vector
    return response.embedding;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Anthropic embedding error:', error);
    throw new Error(`Anthropic embedding failed: ${(error as Error).message}`);
  }
}

/**
 * Truncate long texts to fit within token limits
 * Anthropic's embedding models typically have a token limit
 */
export function truncateForEmbedding(text: string, maxLength = 8000): string {
  // Simple truncation by character count
  // For production, consider more sophisticated truncation based on token count
  if (text.length <= maxLength) {
    return text;
  }

  return text.substring(0, maxLength);
}
```

These implementations provide:
- Functions for generating embeddings from both OpenAI and Anthropic
- Error handling and logging
- Text truncation to handle token limits
- Clean interfaces for embedding generation

<a id="embed-content"></a>
## 7. Embed-Content Script Implementation

Now, let's implement the embed-content script in `/scripts/embed-content.ts`:

```typescript
// /scripts/embed-content.ts
import { connectToDatabase } from '../lib/db';
import { Lesson } from '../lib/db/models/Lesson';
import { Post } from '../lib/db/models/Post';
import { Session } from '../lib/db/models/Session';
import { batchProcessEmbeddings, EmbeddingProvider } from '../lib/chroma/embed';
import { resetCollection } from '../lib/chroma/client';

// Command line arguments
const args = process.argv.slice(2);
const shouldReset = args.includes('--reset');
const provider = args.includes('--anthropic') 
  ? EmbeddingProvider.ANTHROPIC 
  : EmbeddingProvider.OPENAI;

/**
 * Process lessons from the database
 */
async function processLessons() {
  console.log('Processing lessons...');

  const lessons = await Lesson.find({}).lean();

  const embeddableContent = lessons.map(lesson => ({
    id: `lesson-${lesson._id.toString()}`,
    text: `${lesson.title}\n\n${lesson.description}\n\n${lesson.content}`,
    type: 'lesson' as const,
    metadata: {
      title: lesson.title,
      category: lesson.category,
      tags: lesson.tags,
      createdAt: lesson.createdAt,
      updatedAt: lesson.updatedAt,
    }
  }));

  console.log(`Found ${embeddableContent.length} lessons to process`);

  if (embeddableContent.length > 0) {
    await batchProcessEmbeddings(embeddableContent, provider);
  }
}

/**
 * Process blog posts from the database
 */
async function processBlogPosts() {
  console.log('Processing blog posts...');

  const posts = await Post.find({}).lean();

  const embeddableContent = posts.map(post => ({
    id: `post-${post._id.toString()}`,
    text: `${post.title}\n\n${post.summary}\n\n${post.content}`,
    type: 'blog' as const,
    metadata: {
      title: post.title,
      slug: post.slug,
      author: post.author,
      tags: post.tags,
      published: post.published,
      publishedAt: post.publishedAt,
      updatedAt: post.updatedAt,
    }
  }));

  console.log(`Found ${embeddableContent.length} blog posts to process`);

  if (embeddableContent.length > 0) {
    await batchProcessEmbeddings(embeddableContent, provider);
  }
}

/**
 * Process therapy sessions from the database
 */
async function processSessions() {
  console.log('Processing therapy sessions...');

  const sessions = await Session.find({}).lean();

  const embeddableContent = sessions.map(session => ({
    id: `session-${session._id.toString()}`,
    text: `${session.title}\n\n${session.notes}`,
    type: 'session' as const,
    metadata: {
      title: session.title,
      userId: session.userId.toString(),
      date: session.date,
      status: session.status,
    }
  }));

  console.log(`Found ${embeddableContent.length} sessions to process`);

  if (embeddableContent.length > 0) {
    await batchProcessEmbeddings(embeddableContent, provider);
  }
}

/**
 * Main function to run the embedding process
 */
async function main() {
  try {
    console.log(`Starting content embedding process with ${provider} provider`);

    // Connect to the database
    await connectToDatabase();

    // Reset collection if requested
    if (shouldReset) {
      console.log('Resetting ChromaDB collection...');
      await resetCollection();
    }

    // Process all content types
    await processLessons();
    await processBlogPosts();
    await processSessions();

    console.log('Content embedding process completed successfully');
    process.exit(0);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error during content embedding:', error);
    process.exit(1);
  }
}

// Run the script
main();
```

