<a id="best-practices"></a>
## 8. Best Practices for Vector Database Management

### Chunking Strategy

For long content, consider splitting it into smaller chunks for more precise retrieval:

```typescript
/**
 * Split long text into smaller chunks
 */
export function chunkText(text: string, chunkSize = 1000, overlap = 200): string[] {
  const chunks = [];

  if (text.length <= chunkSize) {
    return [text];
  }

  let startIndex = 0;

  while (startIndex < text.length) {
    let endIndex = startIndex + chunkSize;

    // Try to find a natural break point like a paragraph or sentence end
    if (endIndex < text.length) {
      // Look for paragraph break
      const paragraphBreak = text.lastIndexOf('\n\n', endIndex);
      if (paragraphBreak > startIndex + chunkSize / 2) {
        endIndex = paragraphBreak;
      } else {
        // Look for sentence end
        const sentenceEnd = text.lastIndexOf('. ', endIndex);
        if (sentenceEnd > startIndex + chunkSize / 2) {
          endIndex = sentenceEnd + 1; // Include the period
        }
      }
    }

    chunks.push(text.substring(startIndex, endIndex));

    // Move the start index for the next chunk, with overlap
    startIndex = endIndex - overlap;
  }

  return chunks;
}
```

### Document Preconditioning

Preprocess text to improve embedding quality:

```typescript
/**
 * Preprocess text for better embedding quality
 */
export function preprocessText(text: string): string {
  return text
    .trim()
    .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')      // Normalize whitespace
    .replace(/[^\w\s.,?!-]/g, '')  // Remove special characters
    .toLowerCase();            // Convert to lowercase
}
```

### Metadata Strategy

Use metadata effectively for filtering and organization:

- Include essential metadata for filtering (type, category, tags)
- Add temporal metadata (createdAt, updatedAt) for timeframe filtering
- Include user-specific metadata for personalization
- Keep metadata compact and relevant

### Collection Organization

Consider using multiple collections for different purposes:

```typescript
/**
 * Get or create a specialized collection
 */
export async function getSpecializedCollection(collectionName: string): Promise<Collection> {
  const client = await getChromaClient();

  // Check if collection exists
  const collections = await client.listCollections();

  if (collections.includes(collectionName)) {
    return await client.getCollection({ name: collectionName });
  } else {
    return await client.createCollection({ name: collectionName });
  }
}
```

