12. [Development vs. Production Configuration](#development-vs-production-configuration)

## Environment Setup

First, install the necessary packages:

```bash
npm install openai @anthropic-ai/sdk
```

Set up your environment variables in `.env`:

```
# OpenAI Configuration
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4-turbo
OPENAI_ORGANIZATION=your_org_id_if_applicable

# Anthropic Configuration
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-3-opus-20240229
```

Create a `.env.template` file without actual keys for version control:

```
# OpenAI Configuration
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4-turbo
OPENAI_ORGANIZATION=

# Anthropic Configuration
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-3-opus-20240229
```

## OpenAI Integration

Create the OpenAI client in `/lib/ai/openai.ts`:

```typescript
import OpenAI from 'openai';

// Global types for OpenAI responses
export type OpenAIMessage = {
  role: 'system' | 'user' | 'assistant';
  content: string;
};

// Singleton pattern for OpenAI client
let openaiInstance: OpenAI | null = null;

// Get or create OpenAI client
export function getOpenAIClient(): OpenAI {
  if (!openaiInstance) {
    const apiKey = process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY;

    if (!apiKey) {
      throw new Error('OpenAI API key is not configured');
    }

    const config: OpenAI.ClientOptions = {
      apiKey,
    };

    // Add organization if available
    if (process.env.OPENAI_ORGANIZATION) {
